                                                                                            <p class="word-copy-lh-mb"><a href="https://dpsnyder.us/"><strong>D. P. Snyder</strong></a> is a writer, critic, and translator who focuses on contemporary fiction, poetry, and nonfiction. She has translated works by Mónica Lavín, Alberto Chimal, and Angelina Muñiz-Huberman, among others, into English, and poetry by Ian Boyden and Refat Alareer into Spanish. She has written and spoken extensively on collaborative dynamics and the danger of artificial intelligence in the literary translation ecosystem. She is the former co-director of the PEN America Translation Committee and teaches literary translation at New York University.</p>
